      "writtenOn": "2021-07-19T20:42:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should assert that we aren\u0027t double-rewinding or double-accepting in accept() and rewind(), since that would break us (leaving the error reporter null forever). \n\n    SkASSERTF(fErrorReporter, \"Checkpoint was already accepted/rewound\");\n\n\nCuriosity: why do we do it this way instead of using `setErrorCount` to roll back speculative error reports? I\u0027m not sure why the old way wasn\u0027t sufficient.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 354,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "7bc300ca72107799407460bbbe595b2d4357dc3a",
