        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-19T20:42:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Checkpoint might potentially be accepted even if an error occurred:\n\n    Checkpoint x; /* error occurs */; x.accept();\n\n\nIt seems as if this is just dropping the errors, on (I guess) the assumption that we would only accept a result with no errors. The original intent of the SkSLParser\u0027s Checkpoint class was that you could always accept or rewind the result, whether or not the result was an error. I\u0027m not sure if we actually use that flexibility today, but I\u0027d be disappointed to lose the option.",
